{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N35YxTgXmkBTrhYgZErwXM","type":"tool_result","content":"import { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\nimport { h } from 'preact'\nimport { renderToString } from 'preact-render-to-string'\nimport { define } from '../src/index.js'\nimport { html } from '../src/htm.js'\nimport { toPreact } from '../src/preact.js'\n\n// These tests run under Node with no DOM (see `npm run test:preact-ssr`).\n// They render the `microtags/preact` adapter with Preact's own\n// `renderToString` and compare it with the component's `render` static.\n// Preact orders and quotes attributes its own way, so the host start\n// tags are compared parsed, and the inner HTML as a string.\n\ninterface Host {\n    tag:string\n    attrs:Record<string, string>\n    inner:string\n}\n\nconst _named:Record<string, string> = {\n    amp: '&', quot: '\"', apos: \"'\", lt: '<', gt: '>',\n}\n\nfunction decode (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/&(#x[\\da-f]+|#\\d+|[a-z]+);/gi, (m, e:string) => {\n        if (e[0] !== '#') return _named[e.toLowerCase()] ?? m\n        return String.fromCodePoint(e[1] === 'x' || e[1] === 'X' ?\n            parseInt(e.slice(2), 16) :\n            parseInt(e.slice(1), 10))\n    })\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse one host element: its tag name, its attributes as a decoded\n * name -> value map (a bare attribute is the empty string), and the\n * raw HTML between the start tag and the matching end tag.\n */\nfunction parseHost (s:string):Host {\n    const start = /^<([a-z][-\\w]*)/i.exec(s)\n    if (!start) throw new Error('not an element: ' + s)\n    const tag = start[1].toLowerCase()\n    const attrs:Record<string, string> = {}\n    const re = new RegExp(\n        '\\\\s+([^\\\\s\"\\'>/=]+)' +\n        '(?:\\\\s*=\\\\s*(?:\"([^\"]*)\"|\\'([^\\']*)\\'|([^\\\\s\"\\'=<>`]+)))?',\n        'y'\n    )\n    let i = start[0].length\n    for (;;) {\n        re.lastIndex = i\n        const m = re.exec(s)\n        if (!m) break\n        attrs[m[1].toLowerCase()] = decode(m[2] ?? m[3] ?? m[4] ?? '')\n        i = re.lastIndex\n    }\n    const close = /^\\s*>/.exec(s.slice(i))\n    if (!close) throw new Error('unterminated start tag: ' + s)\n    i += close[0].length\n    const end = `</${tag}>`\n    if (!s.endsWith(end)) throw new Error('no end tag: ' + s)\n    return { tag, attrs, inner: s.slice(i, s.length - end.length) }\n}\n\nconst El = define('preact-ssr-el')\n    .withProps(p => ({\n        n: p.number(),\n        s: p.string(),\n        on: p.boolean(),\n        off: p.boolean(),\n        j: p.json<{ a:string }>(),\n        internal: p.prop(7),\n    }))\n    .render(({ props }) => {\n        return html`<b>${props.n}</b><i>${props.s}</i>` +\n            `<u>${props.internal}</u>`\n    })\n    .setup(() => {})\n\nconst props = {\n    n: 3,\n# ADR-010: Preact owns the host, the element owns its children\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-08\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-005][adr-005] and\n[ADR-009][adr-009] (render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\n`../components` (`@substrate-system/components`) is moving its\ncomponents onto microtags, and they have to work inside Preact apps.\nThat covers a client-only Preact render and a Preact `hydrate` of a\nserver-rendered page. A microtags element placed in a Preact tree\nfails in both server cases.\n\nOn the server, Preact's `renderToString` emits an empty host, such as\n`<number-input min=\"1\"></number-input>`. Preact only knows the host\ntag. It does not know that the component has markup of its own, so\nthe page arrives without the component's input or buttons.\n\nIn the browser, Preact 10's `hydrate` collects every existing child of\nan element it hydrates and removes each child it has no vnode for. The\ncomponent's own markup has no vnode, so even if the server sent it,\n`hydrate` deletes it. The only exception is an element whose vnode has\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Preact leaves that element's children alone.\n\nThe terms below have their `CONTEXT.md` meanings. **Hydration** is the\nintent: attaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the\ndocument. **Adopt** is the mechanism: walking markup against existing\nDOM and binding to it without creating nodes. A microtags element\nhydrates itself when its class is registered. The adapter's job is to\nkeep Preact from undoing that hydration. It does not adopt anything\nitself.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd a `microtags/preact` entry that exports `toPreact(El, options?)`.\nIt returns a Preact component that renders the element's host tag.\nOwnership is split at the host:\n\n- Preact owns the host tag and its attributes.\n- The element owns the host's children.\n\n**On the server**, the adapter builds the host vnode from the\ncomponent's render parts (the `renderParts` static, ADR-009's render\nsupport behind a new registry key). The attributes come from the\nparts' `attrs`, and the parts' `html` goes in through\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. `renderToString` then produces the same\nmarkup as the component's own `render` static. A class whose render\nlink was stripped has no `renderParts`, so the adapter throws an error\nthat names the tag.\n\n**In the browser**, the adapter gives the host one shared, fixed\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` whose `__html` is the empty string. It also\npasses the declared props as vnode props, which Preact assigns as\nproperties because the host defines an accessor for each one. Mapped\nevents are passed as `on<event-name>` props. The mechanism depends on\ntwo branches of Preact's element diff:\n\n1. While hydrating, Preact neither writes `innerHTML` nor removes the\n   element's existing children. The server markup stays and the\n   element adopts it.\n2. Outside hydration, Preact writes `innerHTML` only when the new\n   `__html` differs from the old one. The value never changes, so it\n   is written at most once, on the first non-hydrating render. On a\n   client-only mount that write empties the host once, and the element\n   renders itself when it connects. Later renders never touch the\n   children.\n\nBoth branches were verified in Preact 10.29.7. The `preact` dev\ndependency is pinned, so a Preact change arrives as a deliberate bump,\nand the browser tests (hydrate keeps inner nodes, re-render keeps\nthem, typed input survives) check it.\n\nThe browser build is selected by a `browser` export condition, as\n`microtags/htm` already is, and never imports render support.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\nimport { computed } from 'alien-signals'\nimport { define, bindProp } from 'microtags'\nimport { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { Badge } from './badge.js'\nimport './counter.css'\n\n/**\n * A view of a count it does not own. The buttons emit `increment` and\n * `decrement`; whoever passes `count` decides what they do.\n */\nexport const Counter = define('hydra-counter')\n    .withProps(p => ({\n        count: p.number(),\n    }))\n    .withRefs(r => ({\n        current: r.one<InstanceType<typeof Badge>>(),\n        inc: r.one<HTMLButtonElement>(),\n        dec: r.one<HTMLButtonElement>(),\n    }))\n    .render(({ props, refs, children }) => {\n        return html`\n            <div class=\"current\">\n                <span>Current:</span>\n                <span>\n                    <${Badge}\n                        data-ref=\"${refs.current}\"\n                        class=\"number\"\n                        label=${String(props.count)}\n                    />\n                </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"controls\">\n                <button class=\"dec\"\n                    data-ref=\"${refs.dec}\"\n                    aria-label=\"Decrement\"\n                >-</button>\n                <button class=\"inc\"\n                    data-ref=\"${refs.inc}\"\n                    aria-label=\"Increment\"\n                >+</button>\n            </div>\n            ${raw(children)}`\n    })\n    .setup(ctx => {\n        const label = computed(() => String(ctx.props.count()))\n        // the badge's label reads through to the computed\n        bindProp(ctx.refs.current, 'label', label)\n\n        ctx.on(ctx.refs.inc, 'click', () => { ctx.emit('increment') })\n        ctx.on(ctx.refs.dec, 'click', () => { ctx.emit('decrement') })\n    })","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b72a826-f772-437d-997c-f261418189ce","uuid":"24f436c3-2630-47d2-91ea-9c956691370b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:14:31.120Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\nimport { h } from 'preact'\nimport { renderToString } from 'preact-render-to-string'\nimport { define } from '../src/index.js'\nimport { html } from '../src/htm.js'\nimport { toPreact } from '../src/preact.js'\n\n// These tests run under Node with no DOM (see `npm run test:preact-ssr`).\n// They render the `microtags/preact` adapter with Preact's own\n// `renderToString` and compare it with the component's `render` static.\n// Preact orders and quotes attributes its own way, so the host start\n// tags are compared parsed, and the inner HTML as a string.\n\ninterface Host {\n    tag:string\n    attrs:Record<string, string>\n    inner:string\n}\n\nconst _named:Record<string, string> = {\n    amp: '&', quot: '\"', apos: \"'\", lt: '<', gt: '>',\n}\n\nfunction decode (s:string):string {\n    return s.replace(/&(#x[\\da-f]+|#\\d+|[a-z]+);/gi, (m, e:string) => {\n        if (e[0] !== '#') return _named[e.toLowerCase()] ?? m\n        return String.fromCodePoint(e[1] === 'x' || e[1] === 'X' ?\n            parseInt(e.slice(2), 16) :\n            parseInt(e.slice(1), 10))\n    })\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse one host element: its tag name, its attributes as a decoded\n * name -> value map (a bare attribute is the empty string), and the\n * raw HTML between the start tag and the matching end tag.\n */\nfunction parseHost (s:string):Host {\n    const start = /^<([a-z][-\\w]*)/i.exec(s)\n    if (!start)