{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrsKBHjk1PHojibJMbSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `test/types.ts`: the browser build's `toPreact` type equals the default build's.\n[x] `npm run size` passes with the new browser adapter entry, and `npm run gate` passes.\n\nThe browser build of `microtags/preact` is in place and all eight checklist items are done. `npm run gate` exits 0, with 454 of 454 browser tests passing and every other suite green. The work is in three commits, and `.nightralph/notes.md` is left uncommitted.\n\n- **Adapter (`src/preact.browser.ts`):** it passes the declared props and the passthrough `class`, `id`, `aria-*` and `data-*` props to the host. Each mapped event becomes an `on<event-name>` prop. The host gets one shared `{ __html: '' }` as `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. It reuses the prop splitting and the children throw from ticket 03 and never imports render support.\n- **Tests (`test/preact-browser.ts`, run from `test/index.ts`):** they cover all six browser checklist items. Because the adapter was written in the first slice, items 2 to 6 passed on their first run. To show the tests can fail, I broke the adapter on purpose in four ways (no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, no event wiring, no declared props, no children throw), and each break failed the matching tests.\n- **Types:** `test/types.ts` checks that the browser and default `toPreact` types are equal, both in `src/` and in the built `dist/` files. A dist type never equals a src type, even when they match, so each pair stays within one side.\n- **Build and size:** the `browser` export condition is listed first under `./preact`, and the browser source is in `build-esm` and `build-esm:min` (the min build gets `--external:preact`). The new size entry ignores `preact` and measures the adapter alone at 443 B, so I set the limit to 450 B.\n- **AGENTS.md:** the Preact adapter section now covers how to wire and test the browser build.\n\nOne thing the tests don't cover: core does not render anything into an empty host when it connects. A client-only Preact `render` therefore shows the component's markup only if the component's setup renders it. My test component does this. Worth checking that `number-input` in `../components` does the same.\n\nThe spec's built-bundle check that the browser adapter contains no render support or `preact-render-to-string` isn't in this ticket's checklist, so I didn't add it. A manual grep of `dist/preact.browser*.js` found neither."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":94672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756},"output_tokens":702,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b72a826-f772-437d-997c-f261418189ce","uuid":"1e5758c6-962b-4c31-9dbc-cbdafa77d2d6","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:18:54.991Z","request_id":"req_011CgrsKB5b45LGgBwVzWYWn"}
